 "note": "o2-vol-3 = o2-vol-2 made CPU-only (the tiny by-product network trains on the CPU) because no GPU machine with 150+ threads under $1.20/h turned up in 50 minutes (owner 2026-10-22 night: take risks). O_2 Stage B volume, relaunch (o2-vol-1 never found a machine and its streamed label parts hit the trainer's sidecar race that killed o2-g2arm-2): 22M plain hybrid labels as ten separate stored streams of 2.2M (1.6M random + 0.4M rules-v1 + 0.2M harvested), each with a throwaway tiny network, no streaming training beside the labels. Stage A (D6): plain 6M beat exact 1.5M by a wide margin and volume had not flattened. The real 2048-1024-256 network is trained later from the stored parts (label_inputs) so it can be repeated or varied cheaply on a GPU box. A short smoke stream (harvest path at trick 2 with hybrid labels, never run before) comes first.",
